WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.982
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:03.777 --> 00:00:05.360
INSTRUCTOR: In this
video, we're going

00:00:05.360 --> 00:00:07.700
to discuss how to
view, use, and track

00:00:07.700 --> 00:00:11.150
usage of promotional credits,
such as startup credits,

00:00:11.150 --> 00:00:13.460
and your Google Cloud
billing account.

00:00:13.460 --> 00:00:15.140
Let's get started.

00:00:15.140 --> 00:00:16.970
To view your
promotional credits,

00:00:16.970 --> 00:00:19.040
start in the Cloud Console.

00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:22.690
Use the left-hand navigation to
head to the Building console.

00:00:22.690 --> 00:00:24.440
Choose the billing
account for which you'd

00:00:24.440 --> 00:00:26.930
like to view your
promotional credits,

00:00:26.930 --> 00:00:31.130
then locate the Credits pane in
the bottom right-hand corner.

00:00:31.130 --> 00:00:34.640
Click through to credit details
to see a list of your credits,

00:00:34.640 --> 00:00:37.910
including the credit's original
value, remaining value,

00:00:37.910 --> 00:00:39.740
start date, and end date.

00:00:39.740 --> 00:00:42.500
If the Credits pane does not
appear on the Account Overview

00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:46.100
page, it means that the account
does not have any credits.

00:00:46.100 --> 00:00:49.580
Note-- it may take up to 20
minutes after redeeming credits

00:00:49.580 --> 00:00:51.320
to see them in the console.

00:00:51.320 --> 00:00:54.260
To use credits, make sure
your Google Cloud projects

00:00:54.260 --> 00:00:56.090
are linked to the
billing account which

00:00:56.090 --> 00:00:57.650
has the credits applied.

00:00:57.650 --> 00:01:01.160
Note that promotional credits
apply to future use of Google

00:01:01.160 --> 00:01:03.980
Cloud platform products
and cannot be applied

00:01:03.980 --> 00:01:07.610
retroactively, so you are
responsible for any amount

00:01:07.610 --> 00:01:10.550
accrued prior to the
credits being redeemed.

00:01:10.550 --> 00:01:13.820
Credits are valid for the given
time frame after redemption

00:01:13.820 --> 00:01:17.330
date, which is viewable in the
credit details you saw earlier,

00:01:17.330 --> 00:01:19.220
or when the credits
are fully depleted,

00:01:19.220 --> 00:01:22.660
whichever comes first.

00:01:22.660 --> 00:01:24.610
After you've used
your credits, you

00:01:24.610 --> 00:01:27.670
can track their usage at a high
level on the Cost Breakdown

00:01:27.670 --> 00:01:30.160
tab, or you can
dig a little deeper

00:01:30.160 --> 00:01:32.720
and analyze them
on the Reports tab.

00:01:32.720 --> 00:01:35.410
If you use the Cloud
Billing exports to BigQuery,

00:01:35.410 --> 00:01:37.240
you can analyze
your credit usage

00:01:37.240 --> 00:01:39.440
by un-nesting the Credits field.

00:01:39.440 --> 00:01:42.520
An example query is linked
in the video description.

00:01:42.520 --> 00:01:45.460
Head over to the documentation
to check out more details.

00:01:45.460 --> 00:01:48.810
[MUSIC PLAYING]

